  "lineage": "Houston Texas hip-hop production-style invented by DJ Screw (1971-2000) in early 1990s, in which existing hip-hop tracks are slowed dramatically (typically to 60-70% of original tempo) and chopped (rearranged in cut-and-paste sequence with repeats and skips). DJ Screw's Screwed Up Click crew (including Lil' Keke, Big Moe, Z-Ro, Lil' Flip) defined the canonical roster. Distinguished by the chopped-and-screwed technique's production-method-as-genre identity.",
